   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Relative in the dative",
     "texto": [
      "When the noun is the indirect object (to whom), the relative is **dem** (masculine and neuter), **der** (feminine) and **denen** (plural). Example: **Der Kollege, dem ich helfe, ist nett** (the colleague I help is nice). **Die Frau, der ich das Buch gebe** (the woman I give the book to). Plural: **Die Leute, denen ich schreibe** (the people I write to)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out for the gender",
     "texto": [
      "The relative follows the gender and number of the noun, but the case is marked by the verb of the relative clause. That is why **dem** appears with a masculine noun in the dative, whereas **den** was the masculine accusative relative.",
      "The verb of the relative clause goes at the end: **dem ich helfe**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
